A||||34||GT Bastard||Someone must know the c/r with 3.1 dished pistons and stock Fiero heads...||||4||
Z||000000||GT Bastard||01-11-2001||02:49 PM||||Nobody can seem to give me a straight answer on what my compression ratio with be with the Fed Mogul 3.1 V6 Firebird hypereutectic pistons with stock Fiero heads. I know that it's supposed to be something like 8.75-1 with the Firebird heads, but aren't those aluminum?  If they are, I thought the combustion chambers were smaller.  I don't want to end up with something like 8.1-1 compression.  I might as well build a door stop to throw in there.  The only machine work I have left is to the heads, and I'm wondering how much I'm going to need to mill them, but first I want to find out what my CR is for sure.... Anybody???||||reg||4
Z||000001||Shaun41178||01-11-2001||03:42 PM||||this is what upsets me.  Everyone says it is really low cause of the dish but noone actually cc's them to know for sure.  I did some calculations and based on what I found.  I have an excell file around here somewhere if I can find it i will email it to you.  Or Travis might even have it as I mailed it to him.  either way i will try to get it to you.<P>No the firebird heads have iron heads as well.  the stock firebird pistons have a dish too and Gm even states that with a 3.1 crank and iron heads you need a sltight dish to keep the valves off the piston tops.  It is my understanding also that piston companies don't make pistons with a lower compression ratio then what came from the factory stock.  And if so it is like.1 just to offset the fact that you might need to have the block or heads shaved.  So it would be with my guess that if the firebird 3.1's came with a 8.5:1 Cr then the pistons you have are either 8.5-1 or 8.4-1.  overbore should take you up to maybe 8.6 or 8.7-1<P>if the firebird had 8.9-1 compression from the factory then those pistons will probably be in the low 9 range.<P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR><A HREF="http://members.aol.com/Shaun41178" TARGET=_blank>Preferred Performance</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Shaun41178||01-11-2001||03:52 PM||||Basterd.  Travis is going to mail you that excell sheet.  <P>oh yea and i forgot to mention that I bought the same pistons and i was going to have the machine shop check the CR but I never got the engine built so i dont' know now.  Sorry bout that people.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FST2M6||01-11-2001||04:26 PM||||i'll send that excel file when i get home... it should be somthing like 8.6:1... just get a turbo! and run 15psi... that'll fix you RIGHT up!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 01-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||88formula||01-11-2001||05:33 PM||||I was going to do the 3.1-liter stroker engine but I had the same problem with finding compression ratios. I got answers ranging from 7.6-8.8-1. This is one of the reasons I decided to go with the 3.4-liter engine. With that engine I know I can get 9.7-1 compression with the TDC pistons, which is what I have. <P>Another reason I did not go with the 3.1-liter engine is because it seems everyone I have talked to on this forum that has a stroked 2.8-liter engine in there fiero has not gained any performance over the stock motor except in the low rpm range. Most of the 3.1-liter fiero’s here run the quarter mile in the same time that a stock 2.8 does. This fact suggests to me that those guys with there 3.1-liter engines have very low compression ratios, which may be why they have no more top end power than a 2.8. <P>Hey Travis could you e-mail me that excel spreadsheet.<P>Thanks<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||GT Bastard||01-11-2001||06:33 PM||||Thanks for sending that sheet Shaun and Trav!<P>Summit said they should be good for 8.75-1 with the firebird heads.  If I build a 3.1 V6 with 7.6-1 compression, somebody is going to die(probably some poor innocent machinist.)  I would LOVE to throw a turbo on this b!tch and stomp some nutz but it's just too complicated and expensive for me.  Hey Trav, how do I get a hold of that company that makes thinner head gaskets for the V6?||||reg||1
Z||000006||88formula||01-11-2001||09:04 PM||||The only way to really know what the compression ratio is, is to have the combustion chambers cc'ed. You must also know the head gasket volume, volume of the piston dish, and the deck volume to figure out your compression ratio.||||reg||1
Z||000007||PJ||01-11-2001||09:53 PM||||I looked it up in the OEM manual a while ago.  Stock c/r in 3.1's with iron heads was 8 to 1. At least that is what I remember it being. I distinctly remember it was too low to pursue the stock piston route further. As far as I know all the 3.1's in F-Bodies had iron heads. Consider what you have invested and cc the dam thing so you can sleep at night. I would.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Eric||01-12-2001||01:11 AM||||Well those pistons are in my engine.  I've had this thought lingering in my mind since last year because the thing doesn't run well.  With all the work that was done to it, including a big cam and head porting, there's still no improvement in power as far as I can tell (quarter mile timeslips to back it up).  Bastard, if I were you I'd look into getting some custom forged pistons for that engine.  They will cost $500+, but you will be able to run that engine the way it was meant to.  ||||reg||1
Z||000009||1FST2M6||01-12-2001||08:41 AM||||OK.. after looking for about 40 minutes.. i found it on my friends computer...  according to the chart running the pistons you have 8.8:1 should be what it runs at... which is really low but, givin it's larger displacement you'll be ok.. you buy a cam yet? <P>i'm sending the sheet shortly.. let me meander the forum for a sec...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000010||Eric||01-12-2001||05:56 PM||||It may have nothing to do with cr, but my engine pings on anything less than 89 octane.  That's probably something I could fix with retarding the timing, but it's presently set where the car runs the best.  <P>I really don't know what to think about the engine swap.  The down time was so long that I forgot what the car felt like with the 2.8.  I never really got any good baseline stats with the exception of a few 0-60 times all low to mid 8s.  In certain conditions the car will now accelerate to sixty as fast as 7.5 seconds (measured with gtech).  My best quarter mile was 16.4 @ 80.  My first time at the drag srip, and, as Shaun can attest, I was being easy on the car.  I guess I expected more than what I got, but what I got was not bad.||||reg||1
Z||000011||FIEROGOD||01-13-2001||12:27 AM||||Ok lets keep this simple. We have cast-iron 2.8 heads and cast-iron 3.1 heads. Is their a difference? I have a pontiac transport 3.1 in my car---- it is ok. That is a 3.1 with iron heads. I put a 3.1 out of a 92 lumina car with alumanum heads in a freinds car. I used the stock 2.8 heads. The car is alot slower. Are the 2.8 and 3.1 heads the same? There is a difference between 2.8 heads, its the valves. Carbed 2.8 verses injected 2.8. I am not ready to pull the heads off my car to find out! The machine shops can't seem to answer this question. They and i quote "we don't work on many foreign cars". ||||reg||1
Z||000012||GT Bastard||01-13-2001||08:15 AM||||Also, that car with the Fiero heads is cammed.  Brads stil seems a lot quicker with the Transport motor.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Shaun41178||01-13-2001||04:45 PM||||I think that the pistons are not the problems when people rebuild these engines.  I think people aren't doing something right.  My guess would be in the cam and/or prom tuning.  One they don't dial in the cam timing properly when rebuilding it or they don't use a large enough cam.  Two the engine needs more fuel and air now and is running on a 2.8 prom program.  A special burnt chip will be needed to get the max power out of it.<P>A 2.8 with a high lift cam installed will make about 10 extra hp over stock bringing it up around 150hp from the 140 hp factory rating.  <P>Also a 3.1 liter from the FWD cars like the cavaliers made 160 hp and some were at 140 hp as in the RWD cars like the firebirds with the 3.1's.  My guess would be either the cam or the prom tuning for this.  But the cam used in those FWD 3.1's is the same one that is stock Fiero cam.  So a change in displacement results in a change of a +20 hp according to GM.  So the same should go with a rebuilt 3.1 that you people do with the stock cam.  Do some head work and you might pick up another 10-20 hp depending on how far one goes.  Also the heads in the 3.1's all came with the high output heads like our Fiero heads so there is no difference in any of the iron head engines after 88<P>Travis dynoed his 3.1 and it made 106 peak at the wheels but that was with a very restrictive exhaust.  Hell my 2.8 made 110.  He changed the cat on it and for giggles added an e-ram to see what it would do.  It layed down 158 hp I believe after that.  I would guess the e-ram added a 10-15 hp gain which would put Travis' car at 140 hp or so at the wheels and with a 20% driveline loss equates to about 170 or so hp at the flywheel which isn't that bad.  I don't know how far the engine building went as GT basterd put it in but still 170 hp and I would guess around 190 torque isn't that bad.  Some good head work could get the number up into the 190's also with bolt ons.  Now a approx jump in 30 hp just by changing the cat and exhaust on Travis' car proves that it wasn't setup right and that it needed a bit of tweaking mostly with the exhaust.  Perhaps others exhausts are backed up and too restrictive for a 3.2.  i think the ideal is a 2.5 inch catback if you go with the duals or a 2.25-2.5 if you go single like Travis did.  I met up with Travis about a week ago and as he left the steak and shake he was spinning his tires out and it was with an auto tranny.  Now maybe because it was a chilly morning and he had a set of soft compound wide tires on which would give it less grip at that particular time but man I could barely spin my tires cranking off the nitrous at the line.  I would get a small chirp and thats about it and Travis almost got sideways when he left!  I think that is amazing with an auto tranny.  I wanted to race you on the freeway Trav but I could tell you would have killed me.  I was flooring it at one point just to try and keep up with you.  Its too bad traffic was heavy cause I really would have liked to have lined them up just for plays sake <P>People put all this money into the engine rebuild and then don't have it tuned at a dyno and they say it feels sluggish or what not.  A dyno could tell you exactly what the problem is and where more power can be made.  Don't complain, go to a dyno.  <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A>  is one I think.  I hope that is right Travis  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I loaned Travis a set of intake manifolds and he is going to be doing some hacking on them to see if the upper rpm hp can be improved.  Basically the idea is to shorten the overall runner length of the manifolds.  Results should be up in a month or two.  No hurry Travis  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  ok enough blabbering from me<P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR><A HREF="http://members.aol.com/Shaun41178" TARGET=_blank>Preferred Performance</A>||||reg||1
Z||000014||GT Bastard||01-13-2001||07:39 PM||||Great information Shaun... Travis has a 2.8 through, not a 3.1 V6.  Unless he swapped motors without telling me!  Are you saying Trav made 158hp at the wheels with the cheeto??  With just a cat back and an E-Ram?  Sweet Jesus, my SE only lays down 127hp/159tq to the wheels!  ||||reg||1
Z||000015||Eric||01-14-2001||12:50 AM||||What the hell is an E-Ram? <P>I think the issue of cam timing came up before.  I've never resolved it, and frankly, I don't know what's involved in retiming it (a "professional" engine builder built up the long block).  I've been slowly pluging away at finding out what the potential problems are with my motor.  The restrictive Y pipe was replaced and it helped a little, but it wasn't the culprit.  Travis has the same pistons in his motor I take it?  ||||reg||1
